' ============================================================
' HealthGuard - State Diagrams
' (1) Alert lifecycle   (2) Reminder lifecycle
' ============================================================

@startuml healthguard-state-alert
title Alert state diagram
[*] --> generated : alert engine fires\n(threshold or trend rule)
generated --> unread : row written with status='unread'
unread --> read : user opens it / "Mark as read"
unread --> resolved : user acts on it / "Mark as resolved"
read --> resolved : user marks resolved
resolved --> [*]

note right of unread
  Mirrored into notifications
  (bell badge = unread count).
end note

note bottom of resolved
  Alert wording stays cautious in EN and HI;
  resolving only changes UI state.
end note
@enduml


@startuml healthguard-state-reminder
title Reminder state diagram
[*] --> scheduled : user creates reminder\n(once / daily / weekly)
scheduled --> triggered : node-cron fires at scheduled_at
scheduled --> snoozed : user presses "Snooze 10 min"
triggered --> done : user marks done
triggered --> scheduled : daily / weekly recurrence advances to next occurrence
snoozed --> scheduled : snoozed_until reached and cron re-triggers it
snoozed --> done : user marks done
snoozed --> scheduled : user edits the reminder
done --> [*]
triggered --> [*] : one-time reminder completed

note right of scheduled
  Due check runs every minute
  (CRON_SCHEDULE, default */1 * * * *).
  Each trigger also creates an in-app notification.
end note
@enduml
